00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:59.670
Hey, I can do better than that.

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:05.650
I think you better get up on your horse. We'll forget about the fancy gunplay.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.070
Why, Dash? That was just an accident.

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:12.250
I know, but another one like that and you'll be the first cowboy in history wearing open-toed boots.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:21.150
Easy. Take it easy.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.180
Steady, my fellow. Steady.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.340
If that horse was any steadier, he'd be dead.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.480
Hey, stand back there.

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:29.960
I gotta get down to the movie studio and have some publicity pictures took.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.060
- Hey, how's my saddle look?

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:32.850
- Beautiful.

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:33.960
Adios, amigo.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.900
- Chilly-con-cardy!

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.520
- All right, big fella.

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.400
Up, boy!

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:42.050
- Ha-ho!

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:43.670
- I gotta change that name.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:44.670
- What?

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.060
- Ha-ho, Clyde!

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:47.800
Away!

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:49.020
Pound them hooves!

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.340
Faster, boy, faster!

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.830
Fly like the wind!

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:55.910
- Could I talk you into a slow walk?

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.010
- No, you're just wasting your time.

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:00.000
That horse ain't going nowhere.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:01.100
know that.

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:02.440
Do something.

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:03.300
I got to ride

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:03.840
my mount down

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:04.560
to Mammoth Studios

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:05.200
and sign my

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.100
co-star contract.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.260
Well, I can't

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:07.860
do nothing.

00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:09.180
Clyde's a draft horse.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.040
He won't move

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:10.600
unless he's pulling

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:11.120
a wagon.

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:12.300
A wagon?

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:13.240
Yeah,

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:14.400
that one yonder.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:17.280
Jett,

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:18.230
you can't ride

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:19.010
to the movie studio

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:19.930
pulling that thing.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:20.650
Well, it's either

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:21.710
that or drive the truck.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:22.800
There's a choice

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:23.100
for you.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.080
I'm a cowboy.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.390
I can't drive

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:26.950
a truck down

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:27.790
to the movie studio

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:28.950
and I sure can't

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:29.490
ride a horse

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:30.000
pulling that

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.880
wagon. Well, there's a third way.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.140
You can have the horse pull the truck.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.010
I know a fourth way. You can stay at home.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:37.470
Doggone!

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.990
It's the blasted old wagon up.

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:42.490
Just hope Hopalong Cassidy don't see me.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:44.290
Well, I'll hook it up.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.430
You'll have to ask Cousin Bessie before you go

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:47.880
anywhere. What do you mean?

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:50.750
Well, Clyde won't pull his wagon unless Cousin Bessie's

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.420
riding in it. They've got to be

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:53.860
hair-taring fond of each other.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.600
There's one courtship I don't hold much hope

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:57.660
for. No.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.380
Around this place, anything can happen.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.000
What?

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:01.550
Now, hold on.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:06.060
Do you think that I'm going to ride down to the movie studio through the middle of Beverly Hills,

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:09.380
riding this plow horse, pulling that wagon, with that monkey in it?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.160
What kind of a jerk do you think I am?

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:17.230
Oh, God, I'm busy. Quit making so much noise.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:18.630
I don't want to attract no attention.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:30.000
That monkey, look.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.360
Larry.

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:31.440
How should I know?

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:32.540
She's supposed to be here.

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:37.320
Hasn't even signed a contract, and already she's showing up late.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:47.150
Larry, did you ever use a circus in a picture on this lot?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:48.470
Yeah, a few months ago.

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:50.850
Well, you'd better call them.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.470
I think they forgot their freak show.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.400
Where's our start?

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:57.700
What an eyeful.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:58.970
What a knockout.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.000
Thanks, Vance.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:01.960
Hey, bananas!

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.520
Hey, how'd you know I'd be starved?

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:04.800
Hey!

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:06.900
Oh, it's you again.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:07.800
How's your heartburn?

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:09.340
Jethro?

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.570
Say, what are you doing with that monkey?

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:13.660
Carrying her to her dressing room.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.720
Nothing's too good for the co-star or bachelor sheriff knows best.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:18.220
She's a co-star?

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:19.120
Bessie?

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:22.630
That rare combination of beauty and talent.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.380
What about me?

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.460
What about this outfit I bought for me?

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:29.540
Well, if I were you, I'd hang on to it.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.080
I don't know when they might need a replacement for Captain Kangaroos.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:36.290
No kangaroo? I'm a star.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:39.920
Anybody can tell I belong right here in show business just by looking at me.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.040
Hey, say, mister, I bet you know why I'm here.

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:44.570
Yeah, and you're late.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:49.880
Oh, God!

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:55.300
What have you got, man? Mr. Schlepper. Come in.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:56.560
Jethro's been expecting you.

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:59.960
I hope he wasn't too upset about the misunderstanding over Cousin Bessie.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:02.310
He drove his wagon out of the studio at full gallop.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:05.390
The trash man didn't even have time to empty his second barrel.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:10.760
Jethro's all through wanting to be a co-star and dash a series.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.600
All he cares about now is Bessie making good.

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.380
Oh, what a sweet boy he is.

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:15.800
Sure.

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:18.620
Well, where is Bessie? We have the contracts right here.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.300
Well, just a minute, I'll fetch a ragion.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:21.590
A ragion?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:26.240
That's right, sweetie. I'm Bessie's 10-percenter, Swifty Bodine.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:26.700
Oh!

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:27.560
Oh!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:37.040
Bessie's a pretty good nickname for you. You sure come down them stairs fast.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.200
Will you fetch Bessie?

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:39.920
Sure, boy.

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:45.840
All right. Listen, you two, my client, Cousin Bessie, has got to have co-star billing,

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.230
script approval, and an awful good hairdresser.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:54.810
Plus, she gets 10,000 bananas a week, which I get 10%, or 1,000 of them to eat for myself.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.790
Ridiculous. Well, just get another monkey.

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.730
Well, not like Bessie, you won't. Wait till you see what I've done for her.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:12.570
going to be a real big star that sweet naive little girl quality it's gone she's just another

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:21.270
hollywood glamour push hey wait we can make a deal how about a thousand bananas a week

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:24.610
i'll give you a couple of bunches

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:55.820
to say goodbye to Jed and all his kin. They would like to thank you folks for

00:21:55.820 --> 00:22:00.000
kindly dropping in. You're all invited back next week to this locality

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.740
To have a heapin' helpin' of their hospitality

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:05.920
Hillbilly, that is

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:07.260
Set a spell

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:08.880
Take your shoes off

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.960
Y'all come back now, dear

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:13.700
It's been a FilmWise presentation
